+## v0.15.9.11
+
+Keyboard suppressor during engaged Auto chase (Aaron's chase-scene item #3 -- the last chase-scene work item). Closes out the four-item chase scene cleanup that started 2026-05-12.
+
+### Aaron's design clarification
+
+FF8's default keyboard control set is arrows + W/A/D/X/S. v0.15.9.11 suppresses all of these except S (pause) during engaged Auto chase. Plus the mod's navigation hotkeys -, =, Backspace, \ are suppressed at the dispatch level since they bypass the engine keyboard buffer. Everything else (F-keys for audio/TTS control, mod info hotkeys like V/G/T/L/R/`/M/O) remains functional.
+
+### Two-pronged implementation
+
+**1. Engine keyboard buffer (kbBuf) zeroing -- `src/field_nav_input_hooks.inl::HookedGetKeyState`:**
+
+The pre-existing outer block (unchanged) zeros arrow scancodes (Up=0x48, Down=0x50, Left=0x4B, Right=0x4D) whenever `s_analogOverrideActive` is true. A new nested block gated on `::ChaseAutoPilot::IsEngaged() && ::ChaseDetector::GetChaseMode() == ::ChaseDetector::MODE_AUTO` additionally zeros:
+
+```cpp
+kbBuf[0x11] = 0;  // W (default walk modifier)
+kbBuf[0x1E] = 0;  // A (default rotate/move-left)
+kbBuf[0x20] = 0;  // D (default rotate/move-right)
+kbBuf[0x2D] = 0;  // X (default confirm)
+// 0x1F = S NOT zeroed (pause preserved)
+```
+
+The narrower predicate ensures F9 path-finding and world-map AD (which also use `s_analogOverrideActive` but on non-chase fields) aren't affected.
+
+**2. Mod hotkey dispatch gating -- `src/field_nav_handlekeys.inl::HandleKeys`:**
+
+The four mod navigation hotkeys (-, =, Backspace, \) read via `GetAsyncKeyState`, which **bypasses the engine keyboard buffer entirely**. The kbBuf zeroing doesn't reach them. So a chase-Auto early-return was added at the top of `HandleKeys` after the four key states are read:
+
+```cpp
+bool chaseAutoEngaged = ::ChaseAutoPilot::IsEngaged()
+                     && ::ChaseDetector::GetChaseMode() == ::ChaseDetector::MODE_AUTO;
+if (chaseAutoEngaged) {
+    // Preserve edge-detect state so post-chase presses fire cleanly.
+    s_minusWasDown  = minus;
+    s_plusWasDown   = plus;
+    s_bkspWasDown   = bksp;
+    s_driveWasDown  = drive;
+    return;
+}
+```
+
+The `s_*WasDown` statics are updated before the early-return so post-chase edge detection works correctly (no spurious edge if the user releases mid-chase; clean edge for a fresh press after chase ends).
+
+### What stays accessible
+
+- **F-keys (F1-F12)** for audio/TTS control: dispatched in `dinput8.cpp` and other modules, not affected by either suppression layer.
+- **S (pause)**: not in the kbBuf zero list.
+- **Mod info hotkeys** (V version, G/T/L/R for stat lookups, ` repeat, / help, M menu summary, O EWM, etc.): dispatched outside `HandleKeys` in dinput8.cpp, so the `HandleKeys` early-return doesn't reach them. They remain functional because they're informational and don't disrupt the chase route.
+- **Chase ASK navigation**: `IsEngaged()` requires `s_askAnswered`, so during ASK navigation the predicate is false and X confirm + arrow cursors work normally.
+
+### Predicate consistency
+
+Both layers (kbBuf zeroing in `field_nav_input_hooks.inl` and dispatch gating in `field_nav_handlekeys.inl`) use the same predicate: `::ChaseAutoPilot::IsEngaged() && ::ChaseDetector::GetChaseMode() == ::ChaseDetector::MODE_AUTO`. They activate and deactivate in lockstep with chase auto-pilot's engagement state.
+
+### Implementation
+
+Two-file touch plus header includes:
+
+- **`src/field_navigation.cpp`**: added `#include "chase_auto_pilot.h"` and `#include "chase_detector.h"` BEFORE the `namespace FieldNavigation { ... }` block so the chase namespaces reach the global scope (the `.inl` files are included INSIDE the namespace and reference chase via `::ChaseAutoPilot::` with the global scope operator).
+- **`src/field_nav_input_hooks.inl::HookedGetKeyState`**: nested predicate-gated block zeroing W/A/D/X (S preserved) plus one-time activation log line.
+- **`src/field_nav_handlekeys.inl::HandleKeys`**: chase-Auto early-return after key-state reads, with edge-detect static updates and one-time activation log line.
+
+### Expected v0.15.9.11 BAT
+
+Aaron triggers the chase, picks **Auto**. Chase plays out hands-off as in v0.15.9.10 Auto. During the chase, any of these presses are silently ignored:
+- W (walk modifier) - won't override auto-pilot's walk decision
+- A or D (rotate keys) - won't fight the analog override
+- X (confirm) - won't trigger entity interactions
+- - or = (entity catalog cycle) - won't disrupt the selected navigation target
+- Backspace (GPS toggle) - won't activate guided navigation
+- \ (auto-drive toggle) - already refused with a screen-reader message, now skipped silently
+
+S still pauses. F-keys still adjust audio/TTS. The chase completes through to the Lapin Beach FMV.
+
+For verification in `Logs/ff8_field.log`:
+- `FieldNavigation: [v0.15.9.11] chase Auto kb suppressor active: zeroing W A D X (W=%02X A=%02X D=%02X X=%02X) -- S preserved for pause ...` (one-time, kbBuf side)
+- `FieldNavigation: [v0.15.9.11] chase Auto HandleKeys suppressor active: -, =, Backspace, \ disabled until chase ends` (one-time, dispatch side)
+- All v0.15.9.10 Auto BAT markers still apply: no `[CBF]` lines on chase fields, chase completes.
+
+### Risk
+
+Low. Existing arrow-zeroing block untouched; new nested kbBuf block is additive and predicate-gated. `HandleKeys` early-return preserves edge-detect statics for clean post-chase behavior. If a specific suppressed key turns out to be needed during chase, remove it from the relevant list and re-BAT.
+
