+// Auto chase). The base arrow-zeroing block is preserved unchanged: it fires
+// whenever s_analogOverrideActive is true, which covers F9 path-finding,
+// world-map auto-drive, and chase auto-pilot uniformly. A second tighter
+// suppression block was added underneath: when the player is in an actively
+// engaged Auto chase, additionally zero W, A, D, X scancodes -- FF8's default
+// keyboard controls beyond the arrow keys. S (0x1F, pause) is deliberately
+// preserved so the player can still pause mid-chase. ESC/Space/Return are
+// NOT in FF8's default control set so they're not suppressed at the buffer
+// level (any user with custom bindings that map ESC/Space/Return to chase-
+// relevant actions can flag this for v0.15.9.11.1). The narrower predicate
+// ensures that F9 path-finding (which uses the same analog override but on
