+// affected by the extended suppression.
+//
+// Mod hotkey suppression (the -, =, Backspace, \ keys that affect navigation
+// targets) is handled separately at the HandleKeys dispatch in
+// field_nav_handlekeys.inl, since those keys are read via GetAsyncKeyState
+// (which bypasses the engine keyboard buffer entirely).
+//
+// IMPORTANT: this hook zeros the keyboard *buffer*. Mod accessibility hotkeys
+// (F-keys, V, G/T/L/R, slash, backslash, tilde, etc.) are read via
+// GetAsyncKeyState in mod-owned code paths, which bypasses the keyboard
+// buffer entirely. So zeroing W/A/D/X in the buffer does NOT affect any mod
+// hotkey -- only the engine's own reads of those keys.
 static int __cdecl HookedGetKeyState()
 {
